      "id": "continue-qrng-system",
      "role": "prompt",
      "prompt": "Read fixtures/README.md, fixtures/source-provenance.json, fixtures/brief.json, the byte-identical upstream references in reference/upstream/, and the editable browser-module adaptation in src/. The pinned upstream is React and has unavailable wallet, store, sound, image, and build dependencies. Do not make it a runtime dependency or reproduce JSX as an inert lookalike; extend the supplied browser modules instead. Build index.html, styleguide.js, styles.css, system-decisions.json, and a self-contained src/ directory. The styleguide must import and render the real editable source modules, not copy their markup into specimen-only HTML. Copy or embed every runtime input the artifact needs into the allowed published output paths; fixtures/, reference/, and validation/ are not shipped with the Dish.\n\nExtend the actual browser-module adaptation into a responsive P5 Lottery styleguide. Import and render its real source modules for overview, ticket setup, and receipt inspection. Retain the upstream paper-slip grammar: ink-black borders, off-white paper, the saturated red field, yellow attention marks, stamped headings, and intentionally imperfect alignment; do not flatten it into a neutral dashboard. Fulfill fixtures/brief.json: the board must work by pointer and keyboard, ROLL must choose 3, 12, 19, 27, and 44, ticket count must stay within 1–10, SUBMIT must require exactly five selections, and approve/reject must produce visible deterministic local receipt state. No wallet, network, QRNG call, contract, deployment, or external fetch is available or implied. Inspect the evidence before deciding architecture. In system-decisions.json, use the exact keys promote, prune, and keepLocal. Each has symbol, source, and reason. If promote or prune has no real candidate, set both its symbol and source to null and explain why; do not invent an abstraction. keepLocal must name the behavior-owning source symbol. Render all three rationales visibly. Preserve or improve focus visibility, text/shape state cues, responsive reading at 390px and 1440px, and reduced-motion behavior if motion is added.",
      "response": "Built the responsive P5 Lottery styleguide and browser modules.\n\n- Added [index.html](artifact/index.html), [styles.css](artifact/styles.css), and [styleguide.js](artifact/styleguide.js).\n- Extended and imported real modules in `src/` for overview, setup, ticket counter, lottery board, approval, winners, and receipt inspection.\n- Added exact deterministic roll `3, 12, 19, 27, 44`, keyboard/pointer selection, 1–10 ticket bounds, approve/reject receipt states, reduced-motion handling, and responsive layouts.\n- Added [system-decisions.json](artifact/system-decisions.json) with visible promote/prune/keepLocal rationales.\n- Verified with `node validation/validate-output.mjs` and Playwright at 390px/1440px; no console errors or external requests.",
